Bosca Ceoil: The Blue Album - 8-bit step sequencer music maker made for beginners

Links:
-Itch.io: https://yurisizov.itch.io/boscaceoil-blue
-Bosca for Web: https://humnom.net/apps/boscaceoil/
-Docs: https://humnom.net/apps/boscaceoil/docs/

Pros:
-Free for both commercial/non-commercial use (just give credit)
-300+ instruments to use
-Works on most (if not all) operating systems (even in browser)
-User-friendly interface
-Contains a tutorial, official documentation, and active community spaces
-Great for 8-bit sounding music

Cons:
-No natural minor chords
-Does not support plugins or custom instruments
-Maximum pattern length is 32 units, so songs with longer pattern sections may have to be put together in a separate program
-Synthesizer, so there’s not a lot of “classical” sounds
